{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/CQRS with One Database.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/CQRS with One Database.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"cqrs with one database cqrs with one database","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/CQRS with One Database.md","fileName":"CQRS with One Database.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"CQRS with One Database","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-22 20:53\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[CQRS Query and Read Model Design]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["CQRS Query and Read Model Design","Repository Pattern","Read Model","Command Query Responsibility Segregation","hands-ondomain-drivendesignwithnetcore.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/CQRS with One Database.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/CQRS with One Database.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"cqrs with one database cqrs with one database","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/CQRS with One Database.md","fileName":"CQRS with One Database.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"CQRS with One Database","heading":"CQRS with One Database","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"CQRS with one database separates command and query code paths while both use the same physical store. The command side uses the [[Repository Pattern]] to load and persist aggregates; the query side bypasses those repositories and retrieves [[Read Model]]s efficiently from the existing data. This provides conceptual and implementation separation before adding distributed storage. If scale or shape differences later justify separate stores, the established [[Command Query Responsibility Segregation]] boundary makes that change more deliberate.","tags":["baby"],"links":["CQRS Query and Read Model Design","Repository Pattern","Read Model","Command Query Responsibility Segregation","hands-ondomain-drive